## 0. Definitions

"The Program" means the copyrightable work licensed under this
License, and any derivative works of it.

"You" (or "Licensee") means the individual or entity exercising
rights under this License.

"Convey" means any act of making a copy of the Program, or of a
work based on the Program, available to a third party — including
distribution, publication, sale, or making it accessible over a
network — where that third party can obtain a copy. Mere internal
use, or interaction with the Program solely through a network
without transferring a copy, is not Conveyance.

"Corresponding Source" means the source code needed to generate,
build, install, and run the Program (or the work based on it) in
object-code or executable form, including any interface definition
files and the scripts used to control compilation and installation.
It does not include general-purpose tools, compilers, or operating
system components that are not themselves distributed as part of
the work.

"Qualified Charity" means a charitable organization, recognized as
tax-exempt or equivalent under the law of its jurisdiction (for
example, a 501(c)(3) organization in the United States), whose
publicly stated mission includes the conservation, rescue, or
welfare of koalas (*Phascolarctos cinereus*).

