## 2. Copyleft Obligation

If You Convey the Program, or a work based on the Program, You must
satisfy **one** of the following conditions:

**(a) Source Availability.** Convey the Corresponding Source under
the terms of this License, by any of the following means:

  (i) accompanying the object code with the Corresponding Source
      on the same medium; or

  (ii) accompanying the object code with a written offer, valid for
      at least three years, to furnish the Corresponding Source to
      any recipient, for no more than the cost of physically
      performing the transfer; or

  (iii) making the Corresponding Source available from the same
      place, at no charge, alongside the object code, such that a
      recipient can obtain both together.

**(b) Charitable Alternative.** In lieu of (a), make a monetary
donation of not less than USD $20 (or the equivalent in local
currency) to a Qualified Charity, retain a record of that donation
— a receipt, confirmation email, or equivalent document identifying
the amount, date, and recipient organization — and, within thirty
(30) days of first Conveying the work, mail a copy of that record
by post to:

```
The License Compliance Office
Győr Castle
Bécsi kapu tér 5
9022 Győr, Hungary
```

This obligation is satisfied by the act of mailing; retain your own
proof of postage (a receipt from your postal carrier is sufficient)
as your compliance record. Delivery, receipt, or acknowledgment by
the addressee is not required for compliance and is outside Your
control.

You must also retain the underlying donation record for as long as
You continue to Convey the work, and, on written request from the
Licensor made in good faith and no more than once per calendar
year, provide a copy of it within thirty (30) days.

You may satisfy this obligation once per distinct version of the
work You Convey; you are not required to donate or mail separately
for each recipient.

